  'sl.q.basis': 'Basis', 'sl.q.basisText': 'Total joint length {len} m ({rows} kinds of joint); sealant {litres} L from the TDS yield (320 ml ÷ (width × depth) ÷ 1.2, 20 % loss included) plus {waste} % extra allowance; primer {primer}: one 100 ml can per box of 10 cartridges and two per 6 L pail, the balance in 3.2 kg cans †; backer rod about 1.3 × width, 50 m per roll †; masking tape one run each side, 18 m per roll †; labour from the schedule simulator ({crew} people, {days} days).', 'sl.q.notesTitle': 'Notes', 'sl.q.defaultNotes': ['Quantities are estimated from the manufacturer\'s TDS yields; the actual joint sizes on site govern. Joints 10–20 mm wide, 8–15 mm deep and at least 5 mm thick are the warranted range.', 'Sealant and primer are the manufacturer\'s specified combination; no silicone or modified-silicone on site.', 'Scaffolding, disposal of the removed sealant and painting are excluded (listed separately).', 'Valid 30 days; prices exclude freight and insurance.'], 'sl.q.sign': 'Client approval', 'sl.q.by': 'Quoted by', 'sl.q.dist': 'Good Startup LTD. (authorized agent of Auto Chemical Industry Co., Ltd. for Taiwan)', 'sl.q.items.n': { EX: 'AUTON EXCEED 320 ml cartridge', EXP: 'AUTON EXCEED 6 L pail', CLIO: 'AUTON CLIO NEO 320 ml cartridge', NB101: 'AUTON SEALER 101A-NB 320 ml cartridge', NB101S: 'AUTON SEALER 101A-NB 600 ml sausage', OP2019: 'AUTON PRIMER OP-2019 100 ml (in the box)', OP2019B: 'AUTON PRIMER OP-2019 3.2 kg', OP2020: 'AUTON PRIMER OP-2020 100 ml (in the box)', OP2020B: 'AUTON PRIMER OP-2020 3.2 kg', ROD: 'Backer rod (PE foam)', TAPE: 'Masking tape', labour: 'Application labour', misc: 'Other costs' }, 'sl.q.packs.n': { EX: 'cartridges (10 per box)', EXP: 'pails (2 per box)', CLIO: 'cartridges (10 per box)', NB101: 'cartridges (10 per box)', NB101S: 'sausages (20 per box)', OP2019: 'cans', OP2019B: 'cans', OP2020: 'cans', OP2020B: 'cans', ROD: 'rolls (50 m)', TAPE: 'rolls (18 m)', labour: 'person-hours', misc: 'lot' },
  'sl.cmp.label': 'Comparison', 'sl.cmp.title': 'The AUTON sealant range: which one where', 'sl.cmp.sub': 'The three sealants of this guide, the NON-BLEED QUICK adjustment sealant of the UREAX-HG system, and the two dedicated primers.', 'sl.cmp.heads': ['Product', 'Type', 'Use', 'Properties', 'Packaging', 'Primer', 'Certification and tests'],
  'sl.cmp.rows': [['{EX}', 'One-component high-durability, high-weathering polyurethane sealant (LS polymer, plasticiser-free)', 'Cladding panel joints, window perimeters, PCa / RC induced and movement joints, tile and stone joints; termination of liquid waterproofing', 'Shore A 15; M100 0.24; tensile 2.37 N/mm²; elongation 1,135 %; recovery > 90 %; ±25 %; weathering 6,000 h', '320 ml × 10 (with OP-2019 100 ml, nozzles, brush); 6 L pail × 2', 'OP-2019', 'ASTM C920 class 50; JSIA F☆☆☆☆; 10-year project warranty'], ['{NB101}', 'One-component high-durability polyurethane sealant (non-bleed, paintable)', 'Concrete and ALC joints to be painted, substrate for liquid waterproofing, facade joints; water-treatment structures, culvert joints', 'Shore A 16; M50 0.13; tensile 0.95; elongation 771 %; recovery > 86 %; ±25 %; durability class 9030', '320 ml × 10; 600 ml sausage × 20', 'OP-2020 (or OP-2019)', 'JIS A 5758 F-12.5E-9030; ASTM C920 Class 50 (SGS 2020, GSL 2014, PSB 2004); CNS 6985 (SGS 2014); potable-water contact (SGS 2019); JSIA F☆☆☆☆'], ['{CLIO}', 'One-component high-durability clear polyurethane sealant (LSCL polymer)', 'Penetrations and terminations at louvres, vent caps, ducts, boxes; window perimeters, concrete induced joints; termination of the PROTECT ONE system', 'Shore A 50; M50 0.66; tensile 2.00; elongation 243 %; UV 6,000 h no damage; density 1.05', '320 ml × 10 (with OP-2020 100 ml, brush)', 'OP-2020', 'JSIA F☆☆☆☆; not recommended for cladding panel joints (243 % elongation)'], ['{NBQ}', 'One-component quick-drying polyurethane adjustment sealant', 'Corners, cracks and drain surrounds of the UREAX-HG system (covered by the film)', 'Overcoatable in about 1 h; not UV-resistant (must be covered)', '320 ml × 10', 'OP-2020', 'JAIA F☆☆☆☆'], ['{OP2019}', 'Solvent-borne one-component moisture-curing polyurethane primer', 'Dedicated to EXCEED (and TF2000, SMARTSEAL WJ)', 'Dry 15–30 min; 33 % solids; density 0.96; use within a week of opening', '100 ml can (in the box); 3.2 kg can', '—', 'JSIA F☆☆☆☆ JSIA-001024'], ['{OP2020}', 'Solvent-borne one-component moisture-curing polyurethane primer', 'Dedicated to CLIO NEO, 101A-NB, NON-BLEED QUICK, ULTRACOAT (now PROTECT ONE)', 'Dry 15–30 min; 33 % solids; density 0.96', '100 ml can (in the box); 3.2 kg can', '—', 'JSIA F☆☆☆☆ JSIA-001031']],
  'sl.rel.title': 'Related guides and links', 'sl.rel.sub': 'The other two guides on this site and the manufacturer\'s sealant range.', 'sl.rel.rows': [['{HG}', 'The UREAX-HG liquid waterproofing system: EXCEED terminates its film, NON-BLEED QUICK prepares its substrate.', 'Open the guide', '#/ureax-hg'], ['{PO}', 'The PROTECT ONE clear coating: CLIO NEO is its clear termination.', 'Open the guide', '#/protect-one'], ['Sealant range', 'The manufacturer\'s sealant range (with the colour search and the paint-adhesion list).', 'Manufacturer page', 'https://autochem.co.jp/products/sealing/']],
  'sl.cta.sub': 'Quotations, samples and colour cards, application briefings, warranty applications', 'sl.cta.desc': 'Good Startup supplies the standard method statement, TDS, SDS and warranty checklist in Traditional Chinese and applies to the manufacturer for the project-limited warranty on your behalf.', 'sl.cta.page': 'EXCEED product page (manufacturer)',
  'sl.vs.label': 'Versus', 'sl.vs.title': 'Why AUTON polyurethane — five sealant technologies side by side',
  'sl.vs.sub': 'The sealant market has six chemistries: one-component polyurethane, silicone, modified-silicone / MS (silane-modified polyether), two-part polysulphide, acrylic — and the one-component polyurethane Auto Chemical redefined with its LS polymer and no plasticiser. The tables set them against the published data sheets of Sika, Mapei, Fosroc, Dow, MC-Bauchemie and a JIS-certified Japanese product (accessed September 2026), product named and source linked.',
  'sl.fair': 'Fair play: every figure is a printed TDS value (23 °C); modulus is defined differently from sheet to sheet (M50, M100, secant, elastic modulus) and the table says which; products within a class vary a lot, so representative products are shown. Silicone keeps its advantages on glass, curtain walls and under extreme UV, and the table says so. Check the current TDS before specifying.',
  'sl.vs.cardH': ['Chemistry', 'Application', 'Curing', 'Watch-outs'], 'sl.vs.tag': 'this guide', 'sl.vs.vsTag': 'compared',
  'sl.vs.kpi': [['1,135 %', 'ordinary 1K PU 600–700 % (Sika, Mapei TDS)', 'EXCEED elongation at break (JIS A 1439)'], ['Shore A 15', 'ordinary PU 37–40, MS 24–43, silicone 29', 'EXCEED hardness — the softness of low modulus'], ['6,000 h', 'no weathering hours published for the compared products', 'SWOM accelerated weathering, no abnormality (≈ 30 years)'], ['5 reports', 'third-party reports in Taiwan and Singapore (101A-NB)', 'ASTM C920 Class 50, CNS 6985, potable-water contact']],
  'sl.vs.barsLow': 'lower is softer (low modulus)', 'sl.vs.barsHigh': 'higher is better', 'sl.vs.barsAlt': 'second example of the class', 'sl.vs.barsNA': 'not published', 'sl.vs.matrixTitle': 'Criterion by criterion', 'sl.vs.matrixSub': '20 criteria, from chemistry to warranty. The first column stays put; the table scrolls sideways.',
